{{!--
    "Wichtige Regionen" — the region level of the World → Conflict → Region → Event
    hierarchy.

    Regions are derived, not configured: they are the other Ghost tags appearing on
    this conflict's reports (mykolaiv, donetsk, kharkiv on Ukraine reports). A global
    theme setting could not express a per-conflict list, and per-conflict templates
    would defeat the point of a reusable component, so the data comes from the tags
    the editorial workflow already applies.

    Server-rendered output contains duplicates and editorial vocabulary; deduping and
    filtering happen in assets/js/commentarii-mundi.js, which also rewrites the hrefs
    to /commentarii-mundi/{conflict}/{region}/ when nested URLs are enabled. Without
    JavaScript the section hides itself rather than showing a messy list.

    Parameters:
    * conflictSlug — required
    * limit        — how many recent reports to harvest tags from; pass a literal
--}}
{{#if conflictSlug}}
    {{#get "posts" filter="tag:commentariimundi+tag:{{conflictSlug}}" include="tags" limit=limit as |reports|}}
        {{#if reports}}
            <section class="cm-section cm-regions"
                     data-cm-regions
                     data-cm-region-conflict="{{conflictSlug}}"
                     hidden>
                <h2 class="cm-section-title is-title">Wichtige Regionen</h2>
                <ul class="cm-region-list" data-cm-region-list>
                    {{#foreach reports}}
                        {{#foreach tags}}
                            <li class="cm-region" data-cm-region="{{slug}}">
                                <a class="cm-region-link" href="{{url}}">
                                    {{> "commentarii-mundi/icons/pin"}}
                                    <span class="cm-region-name">{{name}}</span>
                                </a>
                            </li>
                        {{/foreach}}
                    {{/foreach}}
                </ul>
            </section>
        {{/if}}
    {{/get}}
{{/if}}
